<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Las Meninas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1656">1656</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Las Meninas is a painting by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-velazquez">Diego Velázquez</a>, completed in 1656 and now in the Prado in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrid">Madrid</a>. It shows the Infanta Margarita Teresa with her maids of honour and attendants in the painter's studio, with Velázquez himself at his easel and the king and queen reflected in a mirror. Its complex play of viewpoints has made it one of the most studied paintings in Western art.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/las-meninas.jpg" alt="Las Meninas" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Velázquez · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Las_Meninas,_by_Diego_Vel%C3%A1zquez,_from_Prado_in_Google_Earth.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
